{:edb/db-before-t 893 :edb/db-after-t 894 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534206 50 #inst "2026-10-11T17:45:28.591Z" 13194139534206 17592186045417 true] [17592186157269 1038 #edb/ref 17592186414003 13194139534206 17592186045417 true] [17592186157269 1038 #edb/ref 17592186414006 13194139534206 17592186045417 true] [17592186157270 1038 #edb/ref 17592186414005 13194139534206 17592186045417 true] [17592186157271 1038 #edb/ref 17592186414004 13194139534206 17592186045417 true] [17592186157694 1068 #edb/ref 17592186154680 13194139534206 17592186045417 false] [17592186157694 1068 #edb/ref 17592186414000 13194139534206 17592186045417 true] [17592186157694 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534206 17592186045417 true] [17592186157694 1071 "Consider the following matrices:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,J=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,P=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nGiven that $B=PJ{P}^{-1},$ find ${e}^{B}.$" 13194139534206 17592186045417 true] [17592186157694 1071 "Consider the following matrices:\n\n$B = \\begin{bmatrix}5 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}, J = \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}, P = \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nGiven that $B = PJP^{-1}$, find $e^{B}$." 13194139534206 17592186045417 false] [17592186157694 1074 "Given a function $f$ and matrices $A$ and $S,$ where $S$ is invertible, we have\n\n$$\nf(SA{S}^{-1})=S\\cdot f(A)\\cdot {S}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nFor $f(x)={e}^{x}$ and the given matrix $B,$ we have\n\n$$\n{e}^{B}={e}^{PJ{P}^{-1}}=P\\cdot ({e}^{J})\\cdot {P}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nNow, since $J$ is a Jordan block with $3$s on the main diagonal, we have\n\n$$\nf(J)=[\\begin{aligned}f(3) & {f}^{′}(3) \\\\ 0 & f(3)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $f$ is ${f}^{′}(x)={e}^{x}.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n{e}^{J}=[\\begin{aligned}f(3) & {f}^{′}(3) \\\\ 0 & f(3)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3} & {e}^{3} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nAlso, the inverse of $P$ is\n\n$$\n{P}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 1}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{B} & =P\\cdot ({e}^{J})\\cdot {P}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3} & {e}^{3} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & {e}^{3} \\\\ {e}^{3} & -2{e}^{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{3} & -4{e}^{3} \\\\ {e}^{3} & -{e}^{3}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534206 17592186045417 true] [17592186413954 1043 #edb/ref 17592186414007 13194139534206 17592186045417 true] [17592186413954 1043 #edb/ref 17592186414008 13194139534206 17592186045417 true] [17592186413954 1043 #edb/ref 17592186414009 13194139534206 17592186045417 true] [17592186413954 1043 #edb/ref 17592186414010 13194139534206 17592186045417 true] [17592186413954 1043 #edb/ref 17592186414011 13194139534206 17592186045417 true] [17592186413954 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534206 17592186045417 true] [17592186413954 1045 "Matrix Functions" 13194139534206 17592186045417 true] [17592186413954 1046 #edb/ref 17592186414010 13194139534206 17592186045417 true] [17592186413954 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046673 13194139534206 17592186045417 true] [17592186413954 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048720 13194139534206 17592186045417 true] [17592186413954 1053 #uuid "f7c04eb8-7724-552c-b148-1c56cf42932a" 13194139534206 17592186045417 true] [17592186413955 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}-92 & 62 \\\\ -186 & 125\\end{aligned}]" 13194139534206 17592186045417 true] [17592186413955 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534206 17592186045417 true] [17592186413955 1083 #uuid "086b5f8c-361e-5e84-ba7f-07908a6ffad8" 13194139534206 17592186045417 true] [17592186413956 1080 "1" 13194139534206 17592186045417 true] [17592186413956 1082 #edb/ref 175921860